ng painting classes. Evan is also making changes to live healthier.\n  - fitness goals: Sam finds fitness goals hard to reach due to discomfort limiting movement and is attempting diet changes. Evan stays in shape by going to the gym and driving.\n  - Evan: Evan apologized to his partner for a drunken night and for accidentally damaging rose bushes, promising to be more careful. He is now looking for low-impact exercises.\n  - Evan: Evan's partner understood his accidental damage to rose bushes. He also enjoys yoga for stress/flexibility and rewatching The Godfather; he previously drank too much with friends.\n  - Evan: Evan recently bought a new Prius that broke down, causing stress. Evan is also considering trying yoga for stress relief and flexibility.\n  - Evan: Evan congratulated Sam on becoming a Weight Watchers coach and expressed excitement for Sam's health journey.\n  - Evan: Evan told his extended family about his marriage and plans to try poutine in Canada next month. He told Sam he had too much to drink last night and did something regrettable involving roses.\n  - Evan: Evan's son hurt his ankle in a soccer accident last Saturday, requiring doctor visits. He expressed interest in healthy recipes Sam learned in cooking class.\n  - Evan: Evan married his partner last week. Evan was asked by Sam if his spouse is the woman from Canada. Evan had previously mentioned enjoying books, painting, driving, and hiking.\n  - something new: Evan suggested trying something new, noting that succeeding at it brings a great feeling of accomplishment.\n  - Evan: Evan drank too much, had a pee accident near some roses, and apologized to Sam for the embarrassing incident.\n  - Evan: Evan plans to go on a hike with Sam soon. He recently returned from a morning walk, which he finds helps start the day actively.\n  - yummy new meals: Sam is taking a cooking class to learn healthier meals, and Evan asked how the class is going and if Sam has picked up any yummy new meals.\n  - 