ah if she knows about the certain method Deborah uses. (event_time: 2023-03-22T17:35:00Z)\n  - Mindfulness can be very helpful for Jolene. (event_time: 2023-08-16T14:58:00Z)\n</FACTS>\n\n# These are the most relevant entities\n# ENTITY_NAME: entity summary\n<ENTITIES>\n  - tasks: Jolene is struggling to prioritize tasks while studying. Deborah suggested using the Eisenhower Matrix to categorize tasks by urgency and importance for better organization.\n  - things: Deborah offered to tell Jolene about a method to organize things based on importance and urgency to help with time management.\n  - hobbies and studies: Deborah finds time management and scheduling helpful for balancing hobbies and studies, which Jolene also inquired about.\n  - Pomodoro Technique: Jolene uses the Pomodoro Technique (25 minutes work, 5-minute break) to avoid burnout but still struggles to prioritize tasks, seeking further time management tips from Deborah.\n  - study plan: Deborah suggested using planners or schedulers for time management and offered help with a study plan.\n  - relaxing while studying: Jolene is seeking tips for staying relaxed while studying, mentioning that advice from loved ones helps with challenges, providing balance and strength.\n  - planificar actividades: Deborah mentioned that planning activities can be both good and tough with a busy schedule and asked Jolene for strategies used.\n  - routines: Jolene is seeking new routines. Deborah suggested a gentle yoga flow focused on breathing and grounding to help Jolene cope, and offered to send a tutorial video.\n  - planners: Jolene started using a bullet journal to track tasks and stay organized as part of her time management strategies.\n  - studying: Jolene has a schedule that includes studying, classes, and personal time, using yoga and meditation for balance.\n  - tips: Deborah offered tips to Jolene for yoga practice, and Jolene thanked her and said she would check them out.\n  - time for myself: Jolene uses brea