nd shared a photo of it at night.\n  - skyline: Calvin took a picture of the stunning skyline in Tokyo last night.\n  - new place: Calvin is exploring his new place, which he describes as a dream come true, after finishing a tour with a well-known artist that ended in Japan.\n  - Times Square: Calvin compared Shibuya Crossing to Tokyo's Times Square while discussing visiting Shinjuku and exploring the area's amazing food.\n  - show in Japan: Calvin had an amazing experience touring with a well-known artist, concluding with a show in Japan.\n  - Shinjuku: Dave mentioned Shinjuku as a cool spot in Tokyo where the food is great, and he is looking forward to exploring it. Calvin was excited to explore Shinjuku in Tokyo and noted there is amazing food there.\n  - podcast: Calvin recorded a podcast following a studio session with Frank Ocean in Tokyo; Dave is excited to hear it when it's uploaded.\n  - Frank Ocean tour: Calvin met Frank Ocean at a Tokyo music festival; they spoke, shared ideas, met again, and recorded a song in the studio at Calvin's mansion.\n  - nice place: Calvin is heading to a nice place next month and will be staying there.\n  - next month: Calvin is heading to a nice place next month and staying there during the trip.\n  - studio: Calvin's music studio was complimented by Dave. Calvin recorded a song with Frank Ocean there after meeting at a Tokyo music festival; it also has a cozy relaxation room.\n  - Japanese culture: Calvin is stuck with his music creativity but is loving getting to know Japanese culture.\n  - mansion: Calvin threw a party for his new album at his Japanese house/mansion, following a prior event where he recorded a song there after meeting Frank Ocean.\n  - Japanese garden: Calvin shot a beautiful picture in a Japanese garden and described it as a peaceful and serene spot he wants others to check out.\n  - traditions: Calvin is fascinated by traditions and cannot wait to experience the culture and taste of a new place.\n  - beac