ost relevant entities\n# ENTITY_NAME: entity summary\n<ENTITIES>\n  - writers group: Joanna shared her book with her writers group last week and received great feedback. She recently finished a cute little bookmark for one of the ladies at her writing club.\n  - book: Joanna finished writing and editing her book last week, exploring themes of sisterhood, love, and chasing dreams. The book had previously been shared with her writers group.\n  - awesome characters: Joanna writes about \"wild worlds with awesome characters\" and is now in a writers group, feeling motivated by inspirational people.\n  - supportive group: Joanna joined a writers group described as inspirational, motivating, and supportive, making her feel like she belongs.\n  - success: Joanna congratulated Nate, describing an outcome as a huge success.\n  - people: Joanna shared how rewarding it was to see her written work performed, drawing inspiration from real life and imagination to create characters.\n  - online blog post: Joanna wrote an online blog post about a hard moment in her life. Someone wrote Joanna a letter after reading it, saying her story brought them comfort.\n  - drama: Joanna felt inspired to write a drama after hiking on amazing trails in her town.\n  - \"Finding Home\": \"Finding Home\" is a script Joanna is writing with her writers group about a girl's journey to find her true home. She finds the work rewarding and emotional.\n  - activities you love: Joanna shared that writing projects are going well, describing the experience as a mix of highs and lows, and that her journal is her rock, viewing writing as a huge part of her life.\n  - someone: Someone wrote Joanna a comforting letter last week after reading her blog post about a difficult moment, realizing her words had power.\n  - good ones: Nate asked Joanna to recommend 'good ones' after sharing his recent success in making coconut milk ice cream.\n  - Jo: Joanna (Jo) asked Nate if he celebrated good feedback people are connecting with his writing. Previously, she asked about a couple he met while walking Max.\n  - writing gig: Joanna had an audition yesterday for a writing gig, feeling a mix of excitement and anxiety afterward. Nate previously encouraged her, noting her hard work and passion.\n  - doubt: Joanna expressed a 'tug-of-war of hope and doubt' after finishing her second script, feeling a mix of excitement and terror about her work getting noticed.\n  - sisterhood: Joanna watched a story exploring themes of sisterhood, love, and chasing dreams, which she recommended. She also finished writing her book last week after many late nights and edits.\n  - literature: Joanna advises reading lots, trying different genres, and writing/sharing literature to build understanding and improve through practice and feedback.\n  - acting: Joanna enjoys acting, especially dramas and emotionally-driven films, and might try it if given the opportunity while currently focusing on her writers group.\n  - meetings: Joanna set up meetings with movie producers to discuss her script and vision, which included elements of self-discovery. The meetings went well, leaving her feeling hopeful and inspired.\n  - birthdays: Joanna uses a recipe with almond flour, coconut oil, chocolate, and raspberries, which is her favorite for birthdays and special days.\n  - Writing and creative projects: Joanna is busy with writing projects, which she finds to be a mix of highs and lows. Her journal is a major source of support for her writing endeavors.\n  - happiness: Joanna stated she will always remember moments that bring happiness and reminded Nate that it's important to stay happy and de-stress by doing what makes him happy.\n  - writer: Joanna, identified as a writer, experienced a major setback when her laptop crashed, resulting in the loss of all her work.\n  - books: Joanna visited the library in Woodhaven (Midwest) and saw an old book collection; she previously asked Nate for book recommendations, and Nate is