hn's sentiment about spreading kindness and support, noting it makes a difference when someone feels down.\n  - passion and dedication: Maria noted John's passion and dedication seem perfect for him, as he recently graduated after a worthwhile journey.\n  - John: John joined a fire-fighting brigade and found the training intense but rewarding. He recently had his first call-out where his team helped those in need.\n  - journey: John sees his journey as a symbol commemorating obstacles overcome. Maria joined a gym and is trying kundalini yoga; they plan to motivate each other.\n  - John (assistant): John joined a service-focused online group last week, finding connection and purpose by sharing inspiring stories and advice with like-minded individuals.\n  - John: John went on a mountaineering trip last week with workmates to clear his head. He found comfort in good memories discussed with Maria.\n  - John: John is trying different workout regimes, including considering rock climbing. He acknowledged the importance of staying in shape and expressed belief in the power of supportive people.\n  - a bit of support: Maria stated that 'a bit of support' can make an amazing change and it is really powerful.\n  - John: John joined the fire brigade. He found the training intense but rewarding. He felt their teamwork during their first intense call-out was essential, and his team feels like family.\n  - Maria: Maria is an assistant who spoke with John about his visit to a veteran's hospital and the resilience of the veterans there.\n  - resilience: Maria complimented John on showing resilience and resourcefulness and asked how he felt afterwards.\n  - John: John is enjoying his new, encouraging job and is being inspired by his team. He offers kickboxing, yoga, and circuit training activities.\n  - John: John joined the fire-fighting brigade, was inspired by the dedication and teamwork, and noted that donations helped acquire a new fire truck.\n  - John: John joined the fire-fig