ing difficulty finding dog-friendly spots to rent, as mentioned to Audrey.\n  - Andrew (assistant): Andrew asked Audrey about the tips she received from her dogs' appointment with an animal behaviorist. Andrew suggested visiting a lake near a trail to see the autumn colors.\n  - puppy: Andrew adopted a new puppy named Toby. Andrew shared photos of his puppy playing in the park, which made Andrew and Audrey happy.\n  - Andrew's girlfriend: Andrew's girlfriend creates a safe and fun space for Scout, and she is encouraged to slowly introduce Scout to Toby and Buddy.\n  - picture: Andrew shared a picture of his dog looking happy while hiking, in response to Audrey mentioning getting tips from an animal behaviorist for her dogs.\n  - Monday: On Monday, Andrew and his girlfriend volunteered at a pet shelter, finding the experience rewarding and joyful.\n  - Andrew's GF: Andrew's GF, Toby, played board games with Andrew last Tuesday. Andrew's GF is mentioned in relation to a sweet sweater and possibly visiting a dog park.\n  - Andrew's pup: Andrew's pup is a German Shepherd known for loyalty and smarts. Andrew is going camping with his girlfriend, Toby, and the pup.\n  - Audrey's pups: Audrey made an appointment with an animal behaviorist for her dogs due to abnormal behavior. She also joined a dog owners group to learn better care methods.\n  - farm: Andrew went to a farm with his girlfriend to get fresh vegetables for dinner recently.\n  - pooches: Pooches moved to a new place with a bigger backyard for running and exploring. Audrey calmed her pooch, Precious, by petting, hugging, and speaking calmly; patience and practice help establish bonds with pooches.\n  - cuatro perros: Audrey has cuatro perros (four dogs) whom she loves; she got a tattoo of them on her arm and took them all to the vet, which was chaotic.\n</ENTITIES>\n","context_tokens":2047,"context_chars":8033,"retrieval_duration":0.1824808120727539,"response_duration":7.540980577468872,"total_duration":7.72346