; it was special, safe for self-expression, and empowering.\n  - poetry: Caroline attended a transgender poetry reading where transgender people shared stories, which was special for self-expression and identity celebration.\n  - trans people: Caroline attended a special, empowering transgender poetry reading where trans people shared stories to celebrate identities. Caroline plans counseling for trans people focusing on self-acceptance support.\n  - art: Caroline was inspired by posters at an event full of pride and strength to make some art; Melanie finds art calming and expressive, and Caroline previously made pottery and attended a poetry reading.\n  - LGBTQ+ counseling workshop: Caroline attended an LGBTQ+ counseling workshop last Friday about therapeutic methods for working with and supporting the mental health of trans people.\n  - school event: Caroline attended a school event last week where she discussed her transgender journey and encouraged student involvement in the LGBTQ community, reflecting on her transition started three years ago.\n  - pride parade: Caroline attended a pride parade last Friday, describing it as awesome with much energy and love, reinforcing the importance of equality.\n  - safe space: Caroline attended an LGBTQ+ counseling workshop last Friday where pros were passionate about making a safe space for trans people.\n  - my own journey: Caroline shared details of her transgender journey, including struggles and development since coming out and starting transition three years ago, at a school event to inspire others.\n  - Caroline's Web: Melanie read \"Charlotte's Web\" as a child and appreciated how it showed the impact of friendship and compassion.\n  - \"Brave\" by Sara Bareilles: Caroline finds \"Brave\" by Sara Bareilles significant as it represents courage and fighting for what is right, reminding her of her progress.\n  - identities: Identities were celebrated and shared through poetry at a transgender poetry reading, creating a